MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Gorilla outdoor tape feels like a natural choice because I have bought Gorilla tape repeatedly, and weather resistance adds a useful benefit for general repairs.",
    "The solder seal connectors fit the wire repair supplies I have bought before; insulating and sealing a wire joint is a practical extension of using crimp connectors."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The battery lugs and half-inch washers require exact cable or hardware sizes that I have no stated need for; being repair supplies alone does not make them useful to me.",
    "Buying a handtruck does not mean I need replacement casters, and my other purchases do not establish a current need for metal-cutting wheels, pocket screws, or strong magnets."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My purchases seem to have been taken as interest in almost any workshop supply, although I choose items for particular repair needs.",
    "My wire connector purchase seems to have been stretched into interest in specialized battery terminals, even though those serve a much more specific application."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated Gorilla tape purchases give a clearer reason to recommend another useful tape variant than my single handtruck purchase gives for recommending wheels.",
    "A useful type of supply is not always something I would buy now: twelve rolls of electrical tape feel excessive this time, and I would try the solder seal connectors before adding a large tubing assortment."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my interest in practical repairs but assumed too many specific project needs from that broad interest."
}
